Z||000000||85ZainoGT||08-14-2001||11:15 PM||||w00000h000000~!!! im happy! I was expecting HIGH 16's to mid 17's, as everyone else prolly was... well I went in my 85gt STOCK AS CAN BE, 4 speed manual, my first time at the track period. ok, so here are the times, from first to third...<P>FIRST RUN<BR>R/T 1.229<BR>60' 2.217<BR>330 6.713<BR>1/8 10.469<BR>MPH 66.17<BR>1000 .000??? lol<BR>1/4 16.475 <BR>MPH 79.14<P>SECOND RUN<BR>R/T .591***<BR>60' 2.257<BR>330 6.673<BR>1/8 10.394<BR>MPH 66.77***<BR>1000 13.547***<BR>1/4 16.276 <BR>MPH 82.20<P>THIRD RUN<BR>R/T 1.152<BR>60' 2.153***<BR>330 6.642***<BR>1/8 10.367***<BR>MPH 66.70<BR>1000 .000(again)<BR>1/4 16.196***<BR>MPH 83.52***<P>so how do you think I did for my first time at the track and it was in my 85gt bone stock...?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||NOS3800||08-14-2001||11:58 PM||||Great work! With alittle practice you can be in the high 15's! What was the weather like? Especially  look at the humidity, high humidity kills times. Heat doesn't help either. Between runs, lay a bag of ice on your air plenum(intake manifold). What was you launching rpm's? Finally, was there any wheel spin? If so, lower your tire pressure to say 27 pounds and see what happens.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||14
Z||000002||Nashco||08-15-2001||12:52 AM||||Great start...if you can get some consistent RTs like your second, and some good 60 foot times, you'll easily get into the 15s!  Good luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||08-15-2001||11:02 AM||||Glad I got something to compare with now. Was wondering if my Fiero ran any good. At the nats recently I ran 9.9 for the 1/8. Consistantly. Wish I had a 1/4 mile track to try it on close by.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000004||85ZainoGT||08-15-2001||01:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NOS3800:<BR><B>Great work! With alittle practice you can be in the high 15's! What was the weather like? Especially  look at the humidity, high humidity kills times. Heat doesn't help either. Between runs, lay a bag of ice on your air plenum(intake manifold). What was you launching rpm's? Finally, was there any wheel spin? If so, lower your tire pressure to say 27 pounds and see what happens.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>as the weather got cooler, I ran better times, humidity is always high here in indy, well most of the time, but ya, I think I can get to 15's nex time I go, I launched at 2000, 2500, and 3000 (1st, 2nd, 3rd) and I had wheel spin on the 3000 in first and second gear...  ill try lowering pressure nex time I go, thanks...||||reg||4
